Third-party works
-----------------

The Chatterbox text-to-speech family
(crates/izwi-core/src/models/architectures/chatterbox) is a Rust port of:

* Chatterbox (https://github.com/resemble-ai/chatterbox)
  Copyright (c) 2025 Resemble AI. MIT License.
* PerTh, the watermarker Chatterbox applies to its audio
  (https://github.com/resemble-ai/Perth)
  Copyright (c) 2025 Resemble AI. MIT License.

and of the parts of these works that Chatterbox builds on:

* CosyVoice (https://github.com/FunAudioLLM/CosyVoice): the S3Gen flow
  decoder and the HiFT vocoder. Copyright (c) 2024 Alibaba Inc.
  Apache License, Version 2.0.
* WeNet (https://github.com/wenet-e2e/wenet) and ESPnet
  (https://github.com/espnet/espnet): the Conformer encoder.
  Copyright (c) 2019 Shigeki Karita; Copyright (c) 2020 Johns Hopkins
  University (Shinji Watanabe); Copyright (c) 2020-2021 Mobvoi Inc.
  Apache License, Version 2.0.
* S3Tokenizer (https://github.com/xingchensong/S3Tokenizer): the speech
  tokenizer used for voice cloning. Copyright (c) 2024 Tsinghua Univ.
  (Xingchen Song) and Dinghao Zhou. Apache License, Version 2.0.
  It is modified from Whisper (https://github.com/openai/whisper),
  Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI, MIT License.
* Matcha-TTS (https://github.com/shivammehta25/Matcha-TTS): the flow
  decoder's U-Net and transformer blocks. Copyright (c) 2023 Shivam Mehta.
  MIT License.
* HiFi-GAN (https://github.com/jik876/hifi-gan): the vocoder's generator.
  Copyright (c) 2020 Jungil Kong. MIT License.
* Snake (https://github.com/EdwardDixon/snake): the vocoder's activation.
  Copyright (c) 2020 Edward Dixon. MIT License.
* CAM++ from 3D-Speaker (https://github.com/alibaba-damo-academy/3D-Speaker),
  as modified in FunASR (https://github.com/modelscope/FunASR): the speaker
  x-vector encoder. Copyright (c) FunASR. MIT License.
* Real-Time-Voice-Cloning (https://github.com/CorentinJ/Real-Time-Voice-Cloning):
  the voice encoder. Modified & original work Copyright (c) 2019 Corentin
  Jemine; original work Copyright (c) 2018 Rayhane Mama. MIT License.

